---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import GlobeHero from "../components/GlobeHero.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Allegra Farrar — Adaptive Sensing for Satellite Monitoring of Tropical Cyclones"
  description="PhD candidate at MIT AeroAstro and the Media Lab, designing adaptive sensing for Earth-observing satellites that watch tropical cyclones and environmental hazards."
>
  <!-- ============================= HERO ============================= -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <span class="eyebrow">MIT AeroAstro &amp; Media Lab &middot; Space Enabled</span>
          <h1>
            Adaptive Sensing Design for
            <span class="grad-text">Advanced Satellite Monitoring</span>
            and Warning of Tropical Cyclones and Environmental Hazards
          </h1>
          <p class="lead mt-16">
            Storms do not wait for the next scheduled overpass. I design Earth-observing
            satellite missions that decide, in real time, where to look — so the
            observations that reach forecasters and regional decision-makers arrive
            early enough to act on.
          </p>
          <div class="flex gap-16 mt-24" style="flex-wrap: wrap;">
            <a class="btn primary frizzle-cursor" href={`${base}/project/`}>
              See the project outline &rarr;
            </a>
            <a class="btn frizzle-cursor" href={`${base}/about/`}>Who I am</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-figure">
          <GlobeHero />
          <p class="figure-note small">
            Satellites pass; only some passes observe. A target lights up when the
            spacecraft decides it is worth the look.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ THE IDEA =========================== -->
  <section class="reveal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">the short version</span>
      <h2>Sensing that reacts to the storm, not to the calendar</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Most Earth-observing instruments collect on a fixed plan and filter hard
        before anything reaches the ground. That works well for building long
        climate records — and badly for catching the hours in which a storm is
        organising. My thesis reworks that decision.
      </p>

      <div class="grid cols-3 mt-40">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-num">01</span>
          <h3>Infer, don't just measure</h3>
          <p>
            A Bayesian network propagates a single observation through coupled
            ocean–atmosphere variables, so the satellite carries an estimate of
            what it does <em>not</em> yet know.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-num">02</span>
          <h3>Act onboard</h3>
          <p>
            A cheap always-on monitor watches for cyclogenesis signatures and
            triggers the expensive inference only when something changes — within
            a small satellite's real power and memory budget.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-num">03</span>
          <h3>Answer to the ground</h3>
          <p>
            The trigger threshold comes from what regional decision-makers
            actually need, not from forecast-skill metrics alone. Usefulness is
            part of the design, not an afterthought.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================= NUMBERS =========================== -->
  <section class="reveal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid cols-4">
        <div class="card center stat">
          <span class="stat-num" style="color: var(--coral);">24 h</span>
          <p class="small">
            average storm awareness time in the Caribbean today
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card center stat">
          <span class="stat-num" style="color: var(--blue);">5 d</span>
          <p class="small">
            lead time CARICOOS needs to prepare for landfall
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card center stat">
          <span class="stat-num" style="color: var(--cyan);">2017–24</span>
          <p class="small">
            CYGNSS operational record the work is built on
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card center stat">
          <span class="stat-num" style="color: var(--sand);">&lt;6 MB</span>
          <p class="small">
            onboard memory footprint the method has to fit inside
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="small mt-16">
        Figures from my JPL SURP seminar; see the project page for sourcing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================= ROUTES ============================ -->
  <section class="reveal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="entry-grid">
        <article class="entry-card">
          <span class="entry-kicker">01 &middot; About</span>
          <h3>Who I am</h3>
          <p>
            Boston-raised, GW-trained, MIT-based. Mars trajectories became hurricane
            sensing. There is an interactive solar system and at least one surprise.
          </p>
          <a class="entry-link frizzle-cursor" href={`${base}/about/`}>
            More about me <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </article>
        <article class="entry-card">
          <span class="entry-kicker">02 &middot; Project</span>
          <h3>What I'm building</h3>
          <p>
            An adaptive sensing framework for Earth-observing satellites: Bayesian
            inference onboard, stakeholder-set thresholds, tested against CYGNSS.
          </p>
          <a class="entry-link frizzle-cursor" href={`${base}/project/`}>
            Read the outline <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </article>
        <article class="entry-card">
          <span class="entry-kicker">03 &middot; Dev log</span>
          <h3>How this site got made</h3>
          <p>
            What I handed to the agent, what I checked myself, and what I threw out —
            logged per session.
          </p>
          <a class="entry-link frizzle-cursor" href={`${base}/devlog/`}>
            Read the log <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(28px, 4.5vh, 56px); }

  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(24px, 4vw, 56px);
  }

  .hero-copy h1 { max-width: 20ch; }

  .hero-figure { position: relative; }

  .figure-note {
    margin: 10px auto 0;
    max-width: 42ch;
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  @media (max-width: 940px) {
    .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .hero-figure { order: -1; }
    .hero-copy h1 { max-width: none; }
  }

  .card-num {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--blue);
    margin-bottom: 9px;
  }

  .stat { padding: 24px 18px; }

  .stat-num {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: clamp(26px, 3.4vw, 36px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .stat p { margin-inline: auto; max-width: 26ch; }

  /* home page route cards, borrowed shape from a bordered 3-up grid */
  .entry-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border: 1px solid var(--card-bd);
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(172, 214, 225, 0.05), rgba(4, 7, 15, 0.2));
  }

  .entry-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 24px 24px 22px;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--card-bd);
    transition: background 0.2s ease;
    position: relative;
  }

  .entry-card:last-child { border-right: none; }
  .entry-card:hover { background: rgba(0, 175, 255, 0.06); }

  .entry-kicker {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--blue);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .entry-card p { flex: 1 1 auto; font-size: 14.5px; margin-bottom: 18px; }

  .entry-link {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--blue);
    margin-top: auto;
    width: fit-content;
  }

  .entry-link::after { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0; }
  .entry-link:hover { color: var(--ink); }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .entry-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .entry-card { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--card-bd); }
    .entry-card:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  }
</style>
